{"data":{"user":{"projectV2":{"items":{"pageInfo":{"hasNextPage":false,"endCursor":"Y3Vyc29yOnYyOpKsMDAwMDAwMDAuMTI1zg4mCG4="},"nodes":[{"id":"PVTI_lAHOALjGtc4Bh5CRzg4mCDE","type":"ISSUE","content":{"__typename":"Issue","number":114,"title":"Config: explicit page slots via a top-level `pages` node","url":"https://github.com/td72/vig/issues/114","body":"## Problem\n\nTab order (the *slot* a page occupies, shown in the header as `n:Label`) is fixed by the registration order in `src/main.rs` and cannot be expressed in the config. Keybindings (`app { \"7\" \"page:worktrees\" }`) address pages by name and are independent of slots, so while a page is missing (e.g. Actions not yet merged) the header reads `6:Worktrees` although the key is `7`. Deriving the header number from the bound key was tried in #113 and rejected: a page is assigned to a slot, and keybindings are operations on that assignment — not the other way round.\n\n## Spec\n\n- New top-level node `pages \"git\" \"github\" \"files\" \"docker\" \"procs\" \"actions\" \"worktrees\"`: the listed order defines slots 1..n and the header shows `n:Label`. When omitted the builtin order applies.\n- A user config's `pages` replaces the builtin list wholesale (same rule as `layout`). Pages not listed are disabled (not registered) — e.g. `pages \"git\" \"files\" \"worktrees\"` gives a three-tab vig.\n- `app { \"<key>\" \"page:<name>\" }` keeps addressing pages by name; the builtin defaults bind each slot number to its page. Bindings to pages that are not in `pages` are an error.\n- The help overlay's \"Switch view\" row is generated from the `app` bindings (`1 / 2 / … / 7`; a user rebinding `\"w\" \"page:worktrees\"` shows `w`).\n- Unknown or duplicate page names in `pages` are errors (fail fast with file and line, like other config errors).\n\n## Tasks\n\n- [ ] `Config::pages()` in `src/core/config/loader.rs` (+ validation in `with_user`, tests)\n- [ ] `merge.rs`: `pages` is a replace-wholesale top-level node\n- [ ] `src/main.rs`: build pages by name, then order / filter them by `pages`; `App` / header consume the slot order\n- [ ] `docs/config.md` (+ README mention), CLAUDE.md \"How to add a page\" (register the name in the builtin `pages` list)\n- [ ] Tests: builtin order, reordering, disabling a page, unknown / duplicate names, binding to a disabled page\n","state":"CLOSED","repository":{"nameWithOwner":"td72/vig"}},"fieldValues":{"nodes":[{"__typename":"ProjectV2ItemFieldRepositoryValue","repository":{"url":"https://github.com/td72/vig","nameWithOwner":"td72/vig"},"field":{"name":"Repository"}},{"__typename":"ProjectV2ItemFieldLabelValue","labels":{"nodes":[{"name":"enhancement"}]},"field":{"name":"Labels"}},{"__typename":"ProjectV2ItemFieldPullRequestValue","pullRequests":{"nodes":[{"url":"https://github.com/td72/vig/pull/117"}]},"field":{"name":"Linked pull requests"}},{"__typename":"ProjectV2ItemFieldTextValue","text":"Config: explicit page slots via a top-level `pages` node","field":{"name":"Title"}},{"__typename":"ProjectV2ItemFieldSingleSelectValue","name":"Done","field":{"name":"Status"}},{"__typename":"ProjectV2ItemFieldDateValue","date":"2026-09-11","field":{"name":"Target date"}}]}},{"id":"PVTI_lAHOALjGtc4Bh5CRzg4mCDk","type":"ISSUE","content":{"__typename":"Issue","number":118,"title":"Fold the Actions page into the GitHub page as a third column","url":"https://github.com/td72/vig/issues/118","body":"## Summary\n\nActions data is GitHub data. Instead of a separate page (key `6`, shipped in v0.7.0), show workflow runs as a third list column of the GitHub page, next to Issues and Pull Requests, with the run's jobs and log in the shared Detail area. One page less, and `gh` detection, disk cache, `o` (open in browser) and search are shared.\n\n```\n┌ Issues ───────┬ Pull Requests ─┬ Workflow Runs ─┐\n│ …             │ …              │ ● CI #191 main │\n├───────────────┴────────────────┴────────────────┤\n│ Detail                                          │\n│  issue → Body / Comments                        │\n│  pr    → Body / Reviews / Comments / Checks     │\n│  run   → Jobs (job → steps tree) │ Log (tail)   │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n## Spec\n\n- GitHub page KDL: add a `runs` pane to `layout` (three list panes on top, default widths 1/3 each, adjustable via `layout`), `tabs \"issues\" \"prs\" \"runs\" \"detail\"`, `bind select=\"runs\" detail=\"detail\"`.\n- `GhDetailContent` gains a `Run` variant; for a run the detail area shows two sub-panes, Jobs (job → steps tree via `core::tree`) and Log (`TailPane`), using the same sub-pane mechanism as the PR detail (Body / Reviews / Comments / Checks). `Enter` on a job or step loads its log; `]` / `[` jump between failed steps.\n- Behaviour carried over from the Actions page: tick refresh while any run is queued / in progress, log polling for running jobs, `o` opens the run in the browser, `/` search.\n- Remove the Actions page: `src/actions/` domain (`client`, `types`, `time`, `log`) and panes move under `src/github/` (e.g. `src/github/actions/…` or `src/github/panes/{runs,jobs,log}.rs`); `page \"actions\"`, `\"6\" \"page:actions\"` and the `actions` entry of `pages` are removed; Worktrees moves to key / slot `6`.\n- A user config that still lists `actions` in `pages` or binds `page:actions` fails fast with a message saying Actions is now part of the GitHub page.\n- Docs: README (Features, view switching, the GitHub View section absorbs the Actions key table), `docs/README.ja.md`, `docs/config.md`; CLAUDE.md architecture line; `tape/demo-github-*.tape` gain the runs column (drop `tape/demo-actions.tape` / `assets/demo-actions.gif` and the `demo:actions` mise task).\n\n## Notes\n\n- Lands in v0.8.0 as \"Actions page folded into the GitHub page\" (v0.7.0 shipped it as a page).\n- Read-only as before: no rerun / cancel.\n","state":"CLOSED","repository":{"nameWithOwner":"td72/vig"}},"fieldValues":{"nodes":[{"__typename":"ProjectV2ItemFieldRepositoryValue","repository":{"url":"https://github.com/td72/vig","nameWithOwner":"td72/vig"},"field":{"name":"Repository"}},{"__typename":"ProjectV2ItemFieldLabelValue","labels":{"nodes":[{"name":"enhancement"}]},"field":{"name":"Labels"}},{"__typename":"ProjectV2ItemFieldPullRequestValue","pullRequests":{"nodes":[{"url":"https://github.com/td72/vig/pull/124"}]},"field":{"name":"Linked pull requests"}},{"__typename":"ProjectV2ItemFieldTextValue","text":"Fold the Actions page into the GitHub page as a third column","field":{"name":"Title"}},{"__typename":"ProjectV2ItemFieldSingleSelectValue","name":"Done","field":{"name":"Status"}},{"__typename":"ProjectV2ItemFieldDateValue","date":"2026-09-14","field":{"name":"Target date"}}]}},{"id":"PVTI_lAHOALjGtc4Bh5CRzg4mCEI","type":"ISSUE","content":{"__typename":"Issue","number":119,"title":"Projects view","url":"https://github.com/td72/vig/issues/119","body":"## Summary\nA read-only page for GitHub Projects (v2), shown as a board. Boards need the full width, so this is a separate page (slot 7 once #118 folds the Actions page into the GitHub page) rather than a column of the GitHub page. Data comes from `gh project list / view / item-list / field-list --format json`.\n\n`gh project` needs the `project` token scope; when it is missing the page shows a notice suggesting `gh auth refresh -s project` instead of failing.\n\n## Non-goals\n- Read-only, like every vig page: no moving items between columns, no field edits, no item creation / deletion.\n\n## Notes\n- Thanks to the `pages` node, users who do not use Projects can drop it from `pages`.\n- Column order follows the `Status` single-select options as ordered on GitHub; items without a status go into a `No status` column.\n- `gh project item-list --limit` is set high (e.g. 500); when truncated the status bar says `(truncated)`.\n- Demo material: a small project linked to a td72 repository (never a real client project).\n\n## Sub-issues\n- #120 — Projects: page skeleton\n- #121 — Projects: project list pane\n- #122 — Projects: board pane\n- #123 — Projects: item detail pane\n","state":"CLOSED","repository":{"nameWithOwner":"td72/vig"}},"fieldValues":{"nodes":[{"__typename":"ProjectV2ItemFieldRepositoryValue","repository":{"url":"https://github.com/td72/vig","nameWithOwner":"td72/vig"},"field":{"name":"Repository"}},{"__typename":"ProjectV2ItemFieldLabelValue","labels":{"nodes":[{"name":"enhancement"}]},"field":{"name":"Labels"}},{"__typename":"ProjectV2ItemFieldPullRequestValue","pullRequests":{"nodes":[{"url":"https://github.com/td72/vig/pull/125"}]},"field":{"name":"Linked pull requests"}},{"__typename":"ProjectV2ItemFieldTextValue","text":"Projects view","field":{"name":"Title"}},{"__typename":"ProjectV2ItemFieldSingleSelectValue","name":"Done","field":{"name":"Status"}},{"__typename":"ProjectV2ItemFieldDateValue","date":"2026-09-07","field":{"name":"Start date"}},{"__typename":"ProjectV2ItemFieldDateValue","date":"2026-09-17","field":{"name":"Target date"}}]}},{"id":"PVTI_lAHOALjGtc4Bh5CRzg4mCEc","type":"ISSUE","content":{"__typename":"Issue","number":120,"title":"Projects: page skeleton","url":"https://github.com/td72/vig/issues/120","body":"## Summary\nFoundation for the Projects page, following the CLAUDE.md \"How to add a page\" checklist.\n\n## Spec\n- `page \"projects\"` in `assets/default.kdl`, `\"7\" \"page:projects\"` in `app { }`, `projects` appended to the builtin `pages` list; `build_pages` arm; loader accessor + test\n- Permission check on first activation: `gh auth status` must include the `project` scope (or the first `gh project` call fails with a scope error) → render a one-line notice (\"gh needs the project scope: run `gh auth refresh -s project`\") instead of the panes; missing `gh` reuses the GitHub page's \"not available\" notice\n- Background fetch via an `mpsc` channel drained in `drain_background()`; disk cache for the project list and the last board (reuse `src/github/domain/disk_cache.rs`)\n- Module layout `src/projects/{mod.rs, page.rs, state.rs, domain/{mod.rs, client.rs, types.rs}, panes/{mod.rs, projects.rs, board.rs, detail.rs}}`\n\nPart of #119.\n","state":"CLOSED","repository":{"nameWithOwner":"td72/vig"}},"fieldValues":{"nodes":[{"__typename":"ProjectV2ItemFieldRepositoryValue","repository":{"url":"https://github.com/td72/vig","nameWithOwner":"td72/vig"},"field":{"name":"Repository"}},{"__typename":"ProjectV2ItemFieldLabelValue","labels":{"nodes":[{"name":"enhancement"}]},"field":{"name":"Labels"}},{"__typename":"ProjectV2ItemFieldPullRequestValue","pullRequests":{"nodes":[{"url":"https://github.com/td72/vig/pull/125"}]},"field":{"name":"Linked pull requests"}},{"__typename":"ProjectV2ItemFieldTextValue","text":"Projects: page skeleton","field":{"name":"Title"}},{"__typename":"ProjectV2ItemFieldSingleSelectValue","name":"Done","field":{"name":"Status"}},{"__typename":"ProjectV2ItemFieldDateValue","date":"2026-09-10","field":{"name":"Start date"}},{"__typename":"ProjectV2ItemFieldDateValue","date":"2026-09-20","field":{"name":"Target date"}}]}},{"id":"PVTI_lAHOALjGtc4Bh5CRzg4mCEk","type":"ISSUE","content":{"__typename":"Issue","number":121,"title":"Projects: project list pane","url":"https://github.com/td72/vig/issues/121","body":"## Summary\nLeft column listing the projects of the repository owner.\n\n## Spec\n- `gh project list --owner <owner> --format json` where `<owner>` is the current repository's owner (org or user); closed projects excluded\n- Rows: number, title, item count, updated (relative); projects linked to the current repository (`gh repo view --json … ` / project `repositories`) are listed first with a marker\n- `/` search over title; selecting a project loads its board (`bind select=\"projects\" detail=\"board\"`)\n- `r` refetches; the list is also refreshed when the page is activated after a while\n\nPart of #119.\n","state":"CLOSED","repository":{"nameWithOwner":"td72/vig"}},"fieldValues":{"nodes":[{"__typename":"ProjectV2ItemFieldRepositoryValue","repository":{"url":"https://github.com/td72/vig","nameWithOwner":"td72/vig"},"field":{"name":"Repository"}},{"__typename":"ProjectV2ItemFieldLabelValue","labels":{"nodes":[{"name":"enhancement"}]},"field":{"name":"Labels"}},{"__typename":"ProjectV2ItemFieldPullRequestValue","pullRequests":{"nodes":[{"url":"https://github.com/td72/vig/pull/125"}]},"field":{"name":"Linked pull requests"}},{"__typename":"ProjectV2ItemFieldTextValue","text":"Projects: project list pane","field":{"name":"Title"}},{"__typename":"ProjectV2ItemFieldSingleSelectValue","name":"Done","field":{"name":"Status"}},{"__typename":"ProjectV2ItemFieldDateValue","date":"2026-09-13","field":{"name":"Start date"}},{"__typename":"ProjectV2ItemFieldDateValue","date":"2026-09-23","field":{"name":"Target date"}}]}},{"id":"PVTI_lAHOALjGtc4Bh5CRzg4mCEo","type":"ISSUE","content":{"__typename":"Issue","number":122,"title":"Projects: board pane","url":"https://github.com/td72/vig/issues/122","body":"## Summary\nKanban board of the selected project, with a table mode.\n\n## Spec\n- Data: `gh project item-list <n> --owner <owner> --format json --limit 500` plus `gh project field-list` to get the `Status` single-select options (column order = option order on GitHub); items without a status form a `No status` column\n- Board mode: columns side by side, each a vertical list of cards — type icon (issue / PR / draft), `#number`, title, assignees; column header shows the option name and card count. `h` / `l` move between columns, `j` / `k` within a column, horizontal scrolling when columns exceed the pane width, `/` search over titles\n- Table mode (`t` toggles): one row per item with the project fields as columns (Status, Priority, Estimate, Iteration, dates, …), sortable by the focused column\n- Selection drives the detail pane; `o` opens the item in the browser; `Enter` / `i` focuses the detail\n- Truncation is surfaced in the status bar\n\nPart of #119.\n","state":"CLOSED","repository":{"nameWithOwner":"td72/vig"}},"fieldValues":{"nodes":[{"__typename":"ProjectV2ItemFieldRepositoryValue","repository":{"url":"https://github.com/td72/vig","nameWithOwner":"td72/vig"},"field":{"name":"Repository"}},{"__typename":"ProjectV2ItemFieldLabelValue","labels":{"nodes":[{"name":"enhancement"}]},"field":{"name":"Labels"}},{"__typename":"ProjectV2ItemFieldPullRequestValue","pullRequests":{"nodes":[{"url":"https://github.com/td72/vig/pull/125"}]},"field":{"name":"Linked pull requests"}},{"__typename":"ProjectV2ItemFieldTextValue","text":"Projects: board pane","field":{"name":"Title"}},{"__typename":"ProjectV2ItemFieldSingleSelectValue","name":"Done","field":{"name":"Status"}},{"__typename":"ProjectV2ItemFieldDateValue","date":"2026-09-16","field":{"name":"Start date"}},{"__typename":"ProjectV2ItemFieldDateValue","date":"2026-09-26","field":{"name":"Target date"}}]}},{"id":"PVTI_lAHOALjGtc4Bh5CRzg4mCEs","type":"ISSUE","content":{"__typename":"Issue","number":123,"title":"Projects: item detail pane","url":"https://github.com/td72/vig/issues/123","body":"## Summary\nDetail of the selected board item.\n\n## Spec\n- Issues and pull requests reuse the GitHub page's detail rendering (Body / Comments); draft issues show their body only\n- A `Fields` section lists every project field value of the item (Status, Priority, Estimate, Iteration, Start / End dates, custom text / number fields)\n- Scrollable like the other detail views; `h` / `Esc` returns to the board\n\nPart of #119.\n","state":"CLOSED","repository":{"nameWithOwner":"td72/vig"}},"fieldValues":{"nodes":[{"__typename":"ProjectV2ItemFieldRepositoryValue","repository":{"url":"https://github.com/td72/vig","nameWithOwner":"td72/vig"},"field":{"name":"Repository"}},{"__typename":"ProjectV2ItemFieldLabelValue","labels":{"nodes":[{"name":"enhancement"}]},"field":{"name":"Labels"}},{"__typename":"ProjectV2ItemFieldPullRequestValue","pullRequests":{"nodes":[{"url":"https://github.com/td72/vig/pull/125"}]},"field":{"name":"Linked pull requests"}},{"__typename":"ProjectV2ItemFieldTextValue","text":"Projects: item detail pane","field":{"name":"Title"}},{"__typename":"ProjectV2ItemFieldSingleSelectValue","name":"Done","field":{"name":"Status"}},{"__typename":"ProjectV2ItemFieldDateValue","date":"2026-09-19","field":{"name":"Start date"}},{"__typename":"ProjectV2ItemFieldDateValue","date":"2026-09-29","field":{"name":"Target date"}}]}},{"id":"PVTI_lAHOALjGtc4Bh5CRzg4mCG4","type":"DRAFT_ISSUE","content":{"__typename":"DraftIssue","title":"Record the Projects demo tape","body":"Draft item used by the vig demo."},"fieldValues":{"nodes":[{"__typename":"ProjectV2ItemFieldTextValue","text":"Record the Projects demo tape","field":{"name":"Title"}},{"__typename":"ProjectV2ItemFieldSingleSelectValue","name":"Todo","field":{"name":"Status"}},{"__typename":"ProjectV2ItemFieldDateValue","date":"2026-09-22","field":{"name":"Start date"}},{"__typename":"ProjectV2ItemFieldDateValue","date":"2026-10-02","field":{"name":"Target date"}}]}}]}}},"rateLimit":{"cost":1,"remaining":4091}}}